{#
  «آراء العملاء» — reviews the merchant types in the customiser.

  | Variable                 | Type    | Description                          |
  |--------------------------|---------|--------------------------------------|
  | component.title          | ?string | Section heading; empty hides it      |
  | component.items[].name   | string  | The reviewer's name                  |
  | component.items[].text   | string  | The review                           |
  | component.items[].stars  | int     | 1–5                                  |
  | component.items[].avatar | ?string | Optional round photo                 |
  | position                 | int     | Sorting number, from zero            |

  WHY THIS SECTION EXISTS. No artboard draws it. Salla's review of 2026-10-20
  asked for "more elements" on Home, and the owner chose (option a) to offer
  the platform's own reviews section restyled in this theme's language rather
  than leave it out. It is merchant-entered, not `salla-reviews`, so it shows
  on a store that has no rating data yet. Derived under B4/B8 — the stories
  panel, the section header and the product card's star row, no new pattern.
  Recorded in /docs/DERIVED-DECISIONS.md.

  Upstream Raed's version (a swiper of 830px slides with a quote glyph and an
  `<h1>`) is replaced whole: it carried a second document heading, a fixed
  width and an avatar with no reserved box.
#}
{% set testimonials_items = component.items|default([]) %}

{% if testimonials_items|length %}
    <section data-testid="store-home-custom-testimonials"
             class="s-block testimonials container"
             {% if component.title %}aria-labelledby="testimonials-{{ position }}-title"{% endif %}>
        <div class="s-block__panel">
            {% if component.title %}
                {% include 'components.ui.section-header' with {
                    title: component.title,
                    align: 'start',
                    level: 2,
                    id: 'testimonials-' ~ position ~ '-title'
                } %}
            {% endif %}

            {# A list, scrolled in CSS like the product row (T-4.03): the reviews
               are siblings, and a screen reader announces how many there are. #}
            <ul class="testimonials__track" role="list">
                {% for item in testimonials_items %}
                    {% set testimonial_stars = item.stars|default(5) %}
                    {% if testimonial_stars > 5 %}
                        {% set testimonial_stars = 5 %}
                    {% elseif testimonial_stars < 1 %}
                        {% set testimonial_stars = 1 %}
                    {% endif %}
                    <li class="testimonials__card">
                        {# The product card's star row, so a rating looks the same
                           everywhere. The stars are hidden from assistive tech and
                           replaced by one sentence, as on the card. #}
                        <div class="product-card__rating testimonials__rating">
                            <span class="sr-only">{{ trans('theme.testimonials.rating', { stars: testimonial_stars }) }}</span>
                            <span class="product-card__stars" aria-hidden="true">
                                {%- for star in 1..5 -%}
                                    <i class="product-card__star{{ star <= testimonial_stars ? ' product-card__star--filled sicon-star2' : ' sicon-star' }}"></i>
                                {%- endfor -%}
                            </span>
                        </div>

                        <blockquote class="testimonials__quote">
                            <p>{{ item.text }}</p>
                        </blockquote>

                        <p class="testimonials__author">
                            {% if item.avatar %}
                                <img class="testimonials__avatar"
                                     src="{{ item.avatar }}"
                                     alt=""
                                     width="40"
                                     height="40"
                                     loading="lazy"
                                     decoding="async">
                            {% endif %}
                            <bdi>{{ item.name }}</bdi>
                        </p>
                    </li>
                {% endfor %}
            </ul>
        </div>
    </section>
{% endif %}
